{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work","id":894035,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Pondering the rest of the work","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-19T08:28:08-07:00","id":894035,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Pondering the rest of the work","content":"Because this is how I do.<br /> <br /> Here's where my brain is at (in terms of notes and road plan) for the rest of Where Fate Has Led, since I've finished at least a first pass on the charms.<br /> Anyone see anything that they're like 'OMG, you can't have a thing about the Sidereals without talking about (bluh)'. Or, conversely, anyone see a section they'd like to see first, or a section they feel should be cut?<br /> <br /> Prologue: Each Age is a Dream That Is Dying<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: Chosen by Destiny<br /> * The Sidereal Exalted and the Maidens of Destiny<br /> ** In the First Age<br /> ** The Usurpation<br /> ** The Shogonate and the Contagion<br /> ** The Time of Tumult<br /> <br /> * The Most Excellent Designers of Destiny and Sidereal Conjunctions (The Bureau of Destiny)<br /> ** The Purpose of Destiny<br /> ** The Golden Barque of Heaven<br /> ** The Cerulean Lute of Harmony<br /> ** The Crimson Panoply of Victory<br /> ** The Forbidding Manse of Ivy<br /> ** The Violet Bier of Sorrows<br /> ** The Loom of Fate<br /> <br /> * Visions Gold and Bronze<br /> ** Ways and Means of the Gold Faction<br /> ** Means and Ends of the Bronze Faction<br /> ** Wandering Stars<br /> <br /> Chapter 2: The Celestial City of Yu-Shan<br /> * The Heart of the City<br /> ** The Jade Pleasure Dome<br /> ** Smaller Diversions<br /> ** Courts of the Incarnae<br /> ** The Fire Exigent<br /> ** Offices and Officers of the Bureau of Heaven<br /> <br /> * The Business of the Gods<br /> ** Commerce in the City of Gods<br /> ** * Quintessence and Ambrosia<br /> ** Peaches of Immortality and Celestial Spirits<br /> ** One Hundred and Eight Gates of Heaven and Earth<br /> ** Offices and Officers of the Bureau of Humanity<br /> <br /> * The Slums of Heaven<br /> ** Idle Gods and Devil's Playthings<br /> ** The Wicked and the Divine (Crime and Law enforcement)<br /> ** Down and Out In the Magic Kingdom<br /> ** Officers and Officers of the Bureaus of the Weather and of Nature<br /> <br /> Chapter 3: Character Creation<br /> * Castes of the Sidereals<br /> * Attributes and Abilities<br /> * Merits<br /> * Division of the Bureau<br /> ** Abilities and Merits<br /> * Charms<br /> * Intimacies and Kismet<br /> * Bonus Points<br /> * Thinking about the Future<br /> <br /> Chapter 4: Traits of the Sidereal Exalted<br /> * Kismet and Paradox<br /> * Merit descriptions<br /> * Caste and Anima Abilities<br /> <br /> Chapter 5: Charms of the Sidereal Exalted<br /> <br /> Chapter 6: Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts<br /> * Sidereal Exalted and Mastery of Martial Arts<br /> <br /> * The Unveiled Arts of Earth<br /> ** Violet Bier of Sorrows Style<br /> ** Shadow Throne Style<br /> ** White Veil Style<br /> ** Mantis Style<br /> ** Celestial Monkey Style<br /> <br /> * The Hidden Arts of Heaven<br /> ** Prismatic Arrangement of Creation<br /> ** Charcoal Marchs of Spiders<br /> ** Citrine Poxes of Contagion<br /> ** Obsidian Shards of Infinity<br /> ** Quicksilver Hand of Dreams<br /> <br /> Chapter 7: Sorcerous Ways and Sidereal Conjunctions<br /> * Arcana of the Sidereal Exalted<br /> ** The Five Station Path<br /> ** Touched By Fate<br /> ** Student of the Book<br /> ** Spells<br /> ** * Walk the Crooked Road<br /> ** * Unbar the Way<br /> ** * Summon the Calibration Gate<br /> <br /> * Astrological Projections<br /> ** Planning the Future<br /> ** Teluric, Supernal and Sidereal Projections<br /> <br /> Chapter 8: Armed and Armored in Starlight<br /> * Sidereals and Evocations<br /> * Artifacts of the Gods<br /> ** Aerial Chariot<br /> ** Cornucopia of Plenty<br /> ** Tiara of Lightning<br /> * Fateful Arms and Armor<br /> ** Sightblinder (Starmetal and Soulsteel Daiklaive, Artifact 3)<br /> ** Wreath of Flowers (Moonsilver and Starmetal Buff Jacket, Artifact 3)<br /> ** Apollyon (Jade Powerbow strung with Starmetal, Artifact 4)<br /> ** Shieldbreaker (Orihalcum and Starmetal Grand Goremaul, Artifact 4)<br /> ** The Cage of the Penient Eidolen Forsaken (Orihalcum and Starmetal Articulated Plate, Artifact 5)<br /> ** The Crimson Aegis of Mars (Starmetal Shield, Artifact 5)<br /> <br /> Chapter 9: The Allies and Enemies of Heaven<br /> * Gods of the Underworld<br /> ** Unlawful Cultist<br /> ** Divine Legbreaker<br /> ** Forbidden God<br /> ** Mastermind Daemon<br /> ** Black Market Extigent<br /> <br /> * Abberations of Fate<br /> ** Impossible Girl<br /> ** Death-in-Life<br /> ** The Traveler in Black<br /> <br /> * The Loyal Opposition<br /> ** Rakan Thulio and the War on Heaven<br /> ** The Getimian Exalted<br /> ** Five Points Fallen, Anterior Caste Getimian<br /> ** Princess Number Eight, Immanent Caste Getimian<br /> ** Shadowed Fortune, Ulterior Caste Getimian<br /> <br /> Epilogue: Or One That Is Coming To Birth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:47:37-07:00","id":894054,"title":"","content":"Wow! That's a great, yet ambitious list. If you need someone to bounce ideas off of, let me know. I'm not that much of a crunchy player, but like Winnie the Pooh, I'm stuffed with fluff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:17:06-07:00","id":894076,"title":"","content":"I want to see (in no particular order) Martial Arts, Spells, and Artifacts/Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"http