rinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:55:01-07:00","id":894122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894117#post894117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Sidereals without Martial Arts are like a person without a head. Or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're... in the list? Chapter 6, Peerless Masters of the Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Durf, or you just mean you'd like to see the martial arts stuff next &gt;&lt; I am red gud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 05-19-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:06:41-07:00","id":894131,"title":"","content":"Or... I didn't actually read your outline, or realize that was a plan of action. Derp.<br /> <br /> You're very ambitious! I had a plan once to write an entire splat book for Werewolf... it's been on my back-burner for years now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Uh... I wasn't going to mention Factions, but since you <i><b>are</b></i> planning to talk about them... I would love to see a vision of them in which they have coherent, plausible plans for keeping Creation intact, especially against threats outside of Fate, instead of &quot;Uh, just keep doing what we did in the Shogunate, nothing can go wrong!&quot; and &quot;Uh, lie to the Solars and just assume they won't go crazy again, nothing can go wrong!&quot; Concrete plans for monitoring and combatting the three realms outside of Fate (Malfeas, Underworld, Wyld) without needing Lunar or Solar help, put into place and given significant priority and resources at least since the Great Contagion. &quot;Sword of Creation &gt;&gt;&gt; Fair Folk army&quot; is a good start but not enough, IMO. By plans, I mean long-running and demonstrably efficacious activities/institutions to actively counter forces outside of Fate, that have been practiced for centuries alongside the Immaculate actions against the Celestials, that PCs can participate in. Also, the Gold Faction should be trying to study if Solars inherently go crazy and if so, why. And really shouldn't be something founded only after the Jade Prison broke. There's no plausible way that there was no dissent whatsoever against the Bronze Vision for 1500 years, even after the Contagion, even from Ayesha Ura. There was stuff they could do before the prison broke (find/break the Prison, gain enough political power to end support for Immaculates and open the Prison, study/protect the remaining Solars, diplomacy with Lunars...) that PCs in historical games ought to have as options. Having no institutional existence before 5 years ago also sets up Gold Faction PCs to have almost zero political backing, monetary resources, mentors, etc. rather than just having significantly less than the Bronze faction.<br /> <br /> I would also be interested in a take on their Great Curse that gives the sense of elders becoming insane and carrying out plans in ways that end up with terrible consequences either for Creation or for the mortals whom they hold themselves aloof from... that somehow doesn't give the impression of <i>stupidity</i> or continue the tradition of the Blind Seers sidebar. Can everything inspired by that sidebar or sharing an aesthetic with it please die in a radioactive green fire? I admit I don't have a good suggestion of <i><b>how</b></i> to depict characters so that they come across in the way I want Sidereal elders to come across... insane, but not dumb. Plans that attract younger ones not just through institutional inertia and political power, but by having an internal logic as well. And younger Sids who are markedly less insane-and-out-of-touch-with-mortals than their elders.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Curse of the Noldor in <i>The Silmarillion</i> might show the sort of thing I'm thinking of -- especially the sense of what went wrong leading to the Fifth Battle, that it wasn't because the elven princes fucked up by stupidity or not considering the obvious, but by making fairly small strategic mistakes in the context of being fated to be betrayed by their followers, and fated to see everything go wrong with their plans that <i><b>could</b></i> go wrong, all at once. This should be doable for Sidereals without huge setting changes, I think -- the Empress vanishing without warning is a good example of &quot;everything going wrong that could go wrong,&quot; coupled with the problems that arise when you make an entire society dependent on one person with a finite lifetime and no heirs, even though there <b><i>were</i></b> cogent reasons to set up the Realm that way that made an internal logic, in the context of the Shogunate infighting that weakened the Dragon-Blooded host.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone else would like to see some of the fanmade Celestial and Sidereal MA converted to 3E. Somebody made a full set of 5 styles (including a tweaked Violet Bier of Sorrows) and there's also a set of 5 &quot;House of [astrological house]&quot; styles created by Sidereals instead of the Maidens. Not having a play-group I wouldn't be using them so I don't feel I can request them, but I wonder if anyone else uses them. I thought they're pretty cool, at least on 'paper.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:45:38-07:00","id":894162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894054#post894054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow! That's a great, yet ambitious list. If you need someone to bounce ideas off of, let me know. I'm not that much of a crunchy player, but like Winnie the Pooh, I'm stuffed with fluff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I pinged you some chapter fic summaries to you, think you'd like a crack at some one page fictions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:58:18-07:00","id":894170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894162#post894162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I pinged you some chapter fic summaries to you, think you'd like a crack at some one page fictions? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe. Depends on if I am inspired by the summaries or not. My muse is a fickle creature at times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:03:25-07:00","id":894175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894131#post894131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or... I didn't actually read your outline, or realize that was a plan of action. Derp.<br /> <br /> You're very ambitious! I had a plan once to write an entire splat book for Werewolf... it's been on my back-burner for years now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Uh... I wasn't going to mention Factions, but since you <i><b>are</b></i> planning to talk about them... I would love to see a vision of them in which they have coherent, plausible plans for keeping Creation intact, especially against threats outside of Fate, instead of &quot;Uh, just keep doing what we did in the Shogunate, nothing can go wrong!&quot; and &quot;Uh, lie to the Solars and just assume they won't go crazy again, nothing can go wrong!&quot; Concrete plans for monitoring and combatting the three realms outside of Fate (Malfeas, Underworld, Wyld) without needing Lunar or Solar help, put into place and given significant priority and resources at least since the Great Contagion. &quot;Sword of Creation &gt;&gt;&gt; Fair Folk army&quot; is a good start but not enough, IMO. By plans, I mean long-running and demonstrably efficacious activities/institutions to actively counter forces outside of Fate, that have been practiced for centuries alongside the Immaculate actions against the Celestials, that PCs can participate in. Also, the Gold Faction really shouldn't be something founded after the Jade Prison broke. There's no plausible way that there was no dissent whatsoever against the Bronze Faction for 1500 years, even after the Contagion, not even from Ayesha Ura. Having no institutional existence before 5 years ago also sets up Gold Faction PCs to have almost zero political backing, monetary resources, mentors, etc. rather than just having significantly less than the Bronze faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my thinking on the Factions goes along as follows;<br /> <br /> The Sidereals have always tended to splinter along 'pragmatic' vs 'idealistic' lines. Well before the Usurpation, these had already earned the monikers of 'Bronze' and 'Gold' factions- although any given Sidereal could and would swing between their stances. As the First Age wore on and the madness of the Solars became more and more evident, the Sidereals cast the Great Prophecy- and the informal factions became hardened. The pragmatic Bronze could not budge on the idea of risking all of Creation; the idealistic Gold could not budge on the idea of ruining Creation to save. Things moved from debate to arguement to a very quiet, very cold civil war. And we all know how things moved from there.<br /> <br /> Since then, only a shadow of the hard faction lines that drove the Usurpation still exist- even ten years ago, the terms 'Gold' and 'Bronze' much more spoke to the idealism / pragmaticism divide again. The return of the Solars has changed that. Sidereals who generally favored idealistic solutions could still look at any given Solar and shudder at what they might do. Pragmatic Bronze Sidereals still might think that the Realm is the right idea- but perhaps with a thin layer of Solar 'puppet masters' whom the Sidereals then manipulate, giving them an extra layer of protection.<br /> <br /> Additionally, a hard core of 'no compromise' Sidereals, calling themselves the 'Copper Dragons' have begun to form- mostly of young Sidereals born on the Blessed Isle after the rise of the Realm, they are only ones who have a 'Kill all Solars' belief verging on the religious.<br /> <br /> (This is also why there's no meaningful discussion of a 'silver' faction, an 'iron' faction, a 'brass' faction- the terms are legacy and refer to ancient yet ongoing political divides, rather than a singular inciting incident over who should rule the world as the Sidereal's puppets)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894131#post894131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also be interested in a take on their Great Curse that gives the sense of elders becoming insane and carrying out plans in ways that end up with terrible consequences either for Creation or for the mortals whom they hold themselves aloof from... that somehow doesn't give the impression of <i>stupidity</i> or continue the tradition of the Blind Seers sidebar. Can everything inspired by that sidebar or sharing an aesthetic with it please die in a radioactive green fire? I admit I don't have a good suggestion of <i><b>how</b></i> to depict characters so that they come across in the way I want Sidereal elders to come across... insane, but not dumb. Plans that attract younger ones not just through institutional inertia and political power, but by having an internal logic as well. And younger Sids who are markedly less insane-and-out-of-touch-with-mortals than their elders.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Curse of the Noldor in <i>The Silmarillion</i> might show the sort of thing I'm thinking of -- especially the sense of what went wrong leading to the Fifth Battle, that it wasn't because the elven princes fucked up by stupidity or not considering the obvious, but by making fairly small strategic mistakes in the context of being fated to be betrayed by their followers, and fated to see everything go wrong with their plans that <i><b>could</b></i> go wrong, all at once. This should be doable for Sidereals without huge setting changes, I think -- the Empress vanishing without warning is a good example of &quot;everything going wrong that could go wrong,&quot; coupled with the problems that arise when you make an entire society dependent on one person with a finite lifetime and no heirs, even though there <b><i>were</i></b> cogent reasons to set up the Realm that way that made an internal logic, in the context of the Shogunate infighting that weakened the Dragon-Blooded host.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the microview, my take on the Sidereal's Curse in play is captured in Paradox, where things starts to get glitchy around the Sidereal because they took Fate into their own hands.<br /> In the macroview, I see no reason to have the Blind Seers. The world is complicated and governed by Murphy- the Sidereals do their best, but like the Second Foundation, they have a damnably hard time dealing with freak incidents outside of their psychohistory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894131#post894131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if anyone else would like to see some of the fanmade Celestial and Sidereal MA converted to 3E. Somebody made a full set of 5 styles (including a tweaked Violet Bier of Sorrows) and there's also a set of 5 &quot;House of [astrological house]&quot; styles created by Sidereals instead of the Maidens. Not having a play-group I wouldn't be using them so I don't feel I can request them, but I wonder if anyone else uses them. I thought they're pretty cool, at least on 'paper.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about it (there's a version of the Golden Barque that I'm rather fond of) but this also seems like a good chance to recapture some of the other popular martial arts style that couldn't make it into the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:25:26-07:00","id":894188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894175#post894175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, <b>a hard core of...Sidereals</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcannon now has a new collective noun for the Chosen of the Maidens. A Hardcore of Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:25:52-07:00","id":894189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894175#post894175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since then, only a shadow of the hard faction lines that drove the Usurpation still exist- even ten years ago, the terms 'Gold' and 'Bronze' much more spoke to the idealism / pragmaticism divide again. The return of the Solars has changed that. Sidereals who generally favored idealistic solutions could still look at any given Solar and shudder at what they might do. Pragmatic Bronze Sidereals still might think that the Realm is the right idea- but perhaps with a thin layer of Solar 'puppet masters' whom the Sidereals then manipulate, giving them an extra layer of protection.<br /> <br /> Additionally, a hard core of 'no compromise' Sidereals, calling themselves the 'Copper Dragons' have begun to form- mostly of young Sidereals born on the Blessed Isle after the rise of the Realm, they are only ones who have a 'Kill all Solars' belief verging on the religious.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good start. For now I have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. If only a young minority wants to murder every Celestial without thought, why did they brainwash the entire Dragon-Blooded host to murder every Celestial without thought, and from the very beginning of the Shogunate?<br /> <br /> 2. What, practically speaking, can &quot;gold&quot;/&quot;idealist&quot; PCs do in a game set before the Jade Prison broke? What form did dissent against the Chejop Kejak plan take? What agendas other than &quot;focus on promoting the Realm and Immaculate Order exactly as it is now, as the top priority&quot; were being persued?<br /> <br /> 3. What have they been doing over the centuries to monitor and be ready to combat forces outside of Fate? What can PCs get involved with on this end, as ongoing projects instead of new initiatives in reaction to the Time of Troubles?<br /> <br /> I feel that, over the entire First Age, the Sidereals were the most vaunted teachers of young Exalted and it couldn't have taken them until the Great Prophecy to get together and say to one another &quot;These Exatled students, they keep going crazy!&quot; Some must have remarked on the limit breaks of Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. And a current of awareness of this would probably be present also in the Second Age, leading not just to a sense of smug superiority over all other Exalted, but also to honest attempts to figure out why this was happening -- including to Solars, since some still existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've also been wondering if the Great Curse, as applied to Sidereals, really needs to take the form of insanity at all. They don't have limit breaks the way the other 3 original Exalted hosts do. Depicting them as making bad decisions in groups can so easily lead to accidentally making them dumb or blind.<br /> In <i>The Silmarillion</i>, the Doom of the Noldor didn't lead to Noldorin elves acting in any way that deserved to be called insane or stupid, even when they made unwise or unethical decisions. They <i><b>all knew</b></i> about the curse, yet it brought their utter ruin anyway. They couldn't just go around it because there was usually no obvious, Point A to Point B, way in which their own actions directly fulfilled it. It influenced their behavior (some elves more than others) but also manifested as things that were fated to happen to them -- their allies betraying them, their plans going awry in the worst possible way, etc. And these things came apart because of their own actions, but in subtle and indirect ways that they didn't easily recognize.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse turned the Solars' great virtues (or great idealism, in 3E) and heroic drive against them, twisting the very qualities for which the Unconquered Sun Chose them into something ruinous. Perhaps it would be appropriate for it to turn the Sidereals' relation to Fate against them by subtly leading to things happening to them, or cascading from the results of their actions, indirectly arising from their own decisions but not manifesting primarily in their plans being <i><b>bad</b></i> ones, or their behavior being insane. Part of it would also be the aloofness from human concerns that is a danger for all Exalted, compounded with alienating effects of the Arcane Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:14:17-07:00","id":894226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894189#post894189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good start. For now I have two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. If only a young minority wants to murder every Celestial without thought, why did they brainwash the entire Dragon-Blooded host to murder every Celestial without thought, and from the very beginning of the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh. It's not exactly- it's more like, your 'average' Bronze Sidereal is open to the idea of working with reality as it is. Reality as it is, is that the Solars are back. Murdering them worked for a long while, but it didn't stick. Whatever the long term projections are, in the short run, it may be better, or even neccesary, to work with some Solars against the dire problems that Creation is facing- with luck, they'll annhiliate each other.<br /> <br /> While the Solars were mostly gone, and as long as the leading cause of Sidereal death is Lunars, the Bronze Faction was totally cool with 'Encourage the Dragonblooded to murder Solars and Lunars', because it was the *easy* thing to do.<br /> <br /> The Copper Dragons don't see it that way. They're a 'No compromise, even in the face of armageddon' group of pragmatic-idealists. To them, the Solars will always be the World's Worst Threat (tm). They grew up (relatively speaking) with idealized versions of the Great Prophecy- they don't internalize the compromises, the philosophical struggle, the urge to reconcile, only the bold speeches of Chejop Kejack and the cowardice of those Goldies that want to compromise with the devil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894189#post894189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What, practically speaking, can &quot;gold&quot;/&quot;idealist&quot; PCs do in a game set before the Jade Prison broke? What form did dissent against the Chejop Kejak plan take? What agendas other than &quot;focus on promoting the Realm and Immaculate Order exactly as it is now, as the top priority&quot; were being persued?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the goal in shifting the faction focus a bit away from the Great Prophecy is to lessen the 'Gold faction Sidereals always oppose Kejak and the Realm, Bronze faction Sidereals always support Kejak and the Realm'. All Sidereals see the Realm and the Immaculate Order as a damned useful tool.<br /> <br /> The difference between the Gold and Bronze Sidereals in the time between the Usurpation and the vanishing of the Empress tends to be... well, more situational. Bronze Faction sidereals tend to prefer the most expedient route to resolving their missions. The sterotype of a Bronze Faction Sidereal is someone who is willing to burn the village to save it; they'll make short term sacrifices for long term gains, is very loss adverse, and prioritizes the goals of the mission over the suffering of Creation. <br /> <br /> Gold Faction sidereals tend to prefer resolving their missions in such a way that it makes the lives of those they touch better- even if they are forgotten, even if the life they touch doesn't matter in the long run. The sterotype of a Gold Faction Sidereal is someone who will gamble the fate of the kingdom on the roll of the dice; they have martyr complexes and will sacrifice themselves to save a handful of mortals, and hate seeing those same mortals suffer. They miss the big picture- they're so concerned with the sickness of a child they overlook the plauge ravaging the city. They're also more prone to going off-mission, taking fate into their own hands, and suffering from Paradox as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894189#post894189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. What have they been doing over the centuries to monitor and be ready to combat forces outside of Fate? What can PCs get involved with on this end, as ongoing projects instead of new initiatives in reaction to the Time of Troubles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spying in Hell (in particular, running covert ops out of Vempura's embassy) and the courts of the Fair Folk. Cultivating contacts with the Liminals.<br /> <br /> I'll confess, I hadn't given these a lot of thought, but will make sure to note something on 'em.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894189#post894189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Curse turned the Solars' great virtues (or great idealism, in 3E) and heroic drive against them, twisting the very qualities for which the Unconquered Sun Chose them into something ruinous. Perhaps it would be appropriate for it to turn the Sidereals' relation to Fate against them by subtly leading to things happening to them, or cascading from the results of their actions, indirectly arising from their own decisions but not manifesting primarily in their plans being <i><b>bad</b></i> ones, or their behavior being insane. Part of it would also be the aloofness from human concerns that is a danger for all Exalted, compounded with alienating effects of the Arcane Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what I'm going for with Paradox. In the spy thriller genre, the spy-protagonist is not usually undone directly by personal failing, but rather by going off mission and/or abusing their authority in some way that sets up a chain of events which bites them in the ass at a critical moment. They don't need the Curse to be 'aloof' from humanity- they live in Heaven and attend parties held out of the Cerulean Lute.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:27:23-07:00","id":894457,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to say, I don't like your version of the Factions now that you get down to details. The idea that there has never been even one single voice of dissent against the Immaculate Faith/Order/whatever or the Wyld Hunt (or the Realm when it existed) for 1500 years, not even from idealists who care about whether innocent people suffer... and your characterization of members of both factions as either willing to burn a village down to save some other village or incapable of even noticing large threats... is really the opposite of what I was hoping for.<br /> <br /> Looks more like Flanderization and a hive-mind to me. :/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894188#post894188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcannon now has a new collective noun for the Chosen of the Maidens. A Hardcore of Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Task Force. I like the idea that due to bureaucratic tradition/inertia, they apply the term to any grouping of Sidereals whether or not they're assigned to work together on any particular task at the moment. Except when they're formally a Convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:11:43-07:00","id":894491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894457#post894457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to say, I don't like your version of the Factions now that you get down to details. The idea that there has never been even one single voice of dissent against the Immaculate Faith/Order/whatever or the Wyld Hunt (or the Realm when it existed) for 1500 years, not even from idealists who care about whether innocent people suffer... and your characterization of members of both factions as either willing to burn a village down to save some other village or incapable of even noticing large threats... is really the opposite of what I was hoping for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm.<br /> <br /> I believe I'm not conveying my ideas well then.<br /> <br /> The core thought is 'move away from the Sidereals being defined by the Usurpation, while still keeping the familiar language'. To me, the idea that Sidereals are motivated and defining themselves by something *other* than the Solars is important. This implies that the Gold and Bronze factions predate the Great Prophecy. They need a divide deep enough that people will recognizably self-sort, but shallow enough that you can believe they'd work together instead of engaging in bloody conflict. It needs to be political, but rooted in philosophy.<br /> <br /> The pragmatic / utilitarian vs idealist divide seemed, to me, like a good candidate for a fit for that.<br /> <br /> The Bronze faction is the faction willing to compromise, to face reality and take things as they are, not as they wish they were- and that often means making hard, ugly choices; it means spying on your friends because one of them is spying on you, and removing the diseased limb to save the patient. Because they play the realpolitik game well, Bronze Sidereals can often accumulate more political power and capital- but at the cost of growing tarnished and crossing lines they swore they would never cross.<br /> <br /> The Gold faction is the faction that is willing to place their faith in things working out. They take great risks which frequently pay off, but when they fail, they fail *spectacularly*. They aren't stupid, but they are trusting in the better angels of everyone's nature, and that no one is so far lost to the darkness that they cannot find the light. They will tend the ailing patient, and many times save both life and limb- but sometimes, the patient dies despite their best efforts. Because Gold Sidereals are more likely to reach a line and say 'Thus far and no farther', they often hit stumbling blocks in their careers, making enemies when a more flexible person could have made an ally- but the Gold Sidereal would rather have a monster as an enemy than an ally anyways, even if that monster does happen to get to decide your operations budget for the next decade.<br /> <br /> The two groups don't come into violent conflict often, because both are ultimately part of the 'Manipulative Secret Masters of the World' club, and both have far more in common with one another than they do differences. Both factions will use any tool they believe they can control- the Realm, the Shogunate, the returning Solars -to achieve their goals, and both believe that their goals will lead to the best Creation possible. Few Sidereals until recently- and them, almost all survivors of the Usurpation -would define themselves as members of their faction... but everyone would know that you could count on certain people to act in a certain way most of the time.<br /> <br /> I mean... I suppose I don't grok what you're looking for, if you don't see how you can have political conflict out of that. From your 'even a single voice of dissent against the Immaculate Faith / Wyld Hunt', I get the feeling you want a more agressively confrontational form of faction politics than I'm envisioning. Which, if so, cool! Not my direction, but that's fine.<br /> <br /> But you would absolutely have Gold faction Sidereals who argue for letting this Solar live a little longer because they're fighting a plague and no one else can do it during the Shogunate. You would also absolutely have Gold faction Sidereals who use the Immaculate Order to push back against the worst impulses of the Dynastic aristocracy in defense of the common folk. And you would have Gold faction Sidereals leading Wyld Hunts against Solars and Lunars that have gone mad and spread death and war like waves on a beach.<br /> You would also absolutely have Bronze faction Sidereals who would love to find a peace with the Lunars, but don't think it's achievable any more and every time someone tries, they *fucking die*. You would have Bronze faction sidereals who disagree about the value of the Empress as an ally, who might have arranged her 'disappearance' to put their own puppet on the throne, or who think that the problem with the *old* Vision of Gold was that the Solars were too old and powerful- but now, with these new, younger, inexperienced Solars...<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the Sidereals (in theory) value the Fellowship above any single faction dispute. The violence that preceeded the Usurpation was an abberation, because the stakes were so high that the pragmatics felt they had no choice. That doesn't mean they don't politic against each other- but it also doesn't mean that they won't use the best tools they can to save the world from itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:51:13-07:00","id":894515,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I prefer the bronze supporting the current Dragonblooded Rule and the Gold pushing for a change to Solar Rule. That way you can have different approaches (idealistic and pragmatic) on either side. <br /> <br /> This way you may get idealistic Bronze Sidereals who believe the Realm Civil War could lead to change away from the Realm's Jade Fist tactics and pragmatic Golds who wish to use Solars and discard them when they go mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:20:30-07:00","id":894526,"title":"","content":"Here are some possible situations I'd like to see :<br /> <br /> 1. Idealistic Bronze faction abolishionist neglects to report a Solar Exaltation for a few weeks in exchange for help destroying a child slavery ring. <br /> <br /> 2. Pragmatic Gold will sometimes ride on Wyld Hunt when the Solar in question has murdered, tortured, etc. Someone has to take the dangerous guilty Solar down. <br /> <br /> Kejak may be a true believer, but every Sidereal has thier own reasons for supporting Gold, Bronze, or none at all. Those reasons may be pure, like &quot;Those Dragonblooded did alright during Baelor's Crusade&quot; or &quot;Killing innocent Solars is wrong&quot; Other reasons could be less pure, &quot;The Bronze Faction never gave me a promotion, so fuck them.&quot; or &quot;I got a pretty sweet gig at the Imperial court. Putting Solars in charge may threaten that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:19:16-07:00","id":894621,"title":"","content":"Seems like your faction divisions relate to much of the way the main political left and right in the UK have drawn their battle lines currently. The Tory party over here presenting themselves as the party of pragmatism. Balancing books, making tough decisions on security, The Left has made a very ideological stand at the moment, anti war and pro disarmament, environmental and social idealism. <br /> <br /> I like this divide as I think it makes interesting politics. What is interesting historically is that both sides are idealistic and stand for something but have presented themselves as either idealistic or pragmatic as circumstance dictates. I think this fluid nature would be more interesting. For example the Bronze are looking incredibly more idealism driven now propping up a state that is showing it isn't working because its their baby, hunting down Solars when they would be great allies against new threats. The Goldstars can actually paint themselves as the pragmatists now to the business of managing creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T05:10:07-07:00","id":894663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894621#post894621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like your faction divisions relate to much of the way the main political left and right in the UK have drawn their battle lines currently. The Tory party over here presenting themselves as the party of pragmatism. Balancing books, making tough decisions on security, The Left has made a very ideological stand at the moment, anti war and pro disarmament, environmental and social idealism.<br /> <br /> I like this divide as I think it makes interesting politics. What is interesting historically is that both sides are idealistic and stand for something but have presented themselves as either idealistic or pragmatic as circumstance dictates. I think this fluid nature would be more interesting. For example the Bronze are looking incredibly more idealism driven now propping up a state that is showing it isn't working because its their baby, hunting down Solars when they would be great allies against new threats. The Goldstars can actually paint themselves as the pragmatists now to the business of managing creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be a liar to say that I wasn't drawing a certain degree of inspiration from several modern political movements. Or that the Copper Dragons weren't tremendous fans of the tea from the Blessed Isle, often hosting parties to celebrate such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:37:30-07:00","id":894765,"title":"","content":"Nah, I don't mean I'd wish to see them physically fighting each other, I think that would make for a poor game. I like the suggestion that the Bronze get their dominance partly from being good at realpolitik (though having massacred the entire Gold Faction during the Usurpation and having 100% of elders on their side has got to be significant, too.)<br /> <br /> But you haven't actually changed the Factions here: you've eliminated them entirely, made everybody Bronze Faction, and then recycled the names for comparatively small differences in philosophy.<br /> <br /> I think there would be disagreement and dissent about policy on the largest scales, not just small local issues. People don't line up unanimously to support the status quo unless it's going <b><i>really </i></b><i><b>well</b></i> and there are easy answers for everything, which it hasn't since at least the mid-First Age. I think it's just not plausible that for 1500 years, all the Sidereals were 100% unanimous about exclusive (and quite oppressive) Terrestrial rule*, even in the immediate aftermath of the Contagion. That even right after the apocalypse not one of them started to think that Terrestrials+Sidereals were inadequate to protect Creation without Solar or Lunar help, and they needed a change of plan. There are reasons for both idealists and pragmatists to argue against the Realm.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean by hive-mind. My opinion may be uncommon on this forum, but if even one Exalted player can have a differing opinion, surely so would at least a one or two Sidereals. They are intelligent, very highly educated individuals who grow up in widely different circumstances, not robots. There are no easy answers for the biggest problems, so people won't all agree how to solve them. 100% agreement is really incomprehensible to me. Humans don't function that way.<br /> <br /> *I think they all would agree on just 2 things: the death of any Sidereal is a bad thing, and that actually <b><i>Sidereals</i></b> should rule the world and everybody else is a puppet or an enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> And like Wonder said, there would likely be pragmatists and idealists on all sides. Bronze Faction idealists who believe the Realm is the best option to defend Creation but try to reform it and end the mass slavery because they want the DBs to be just rulers, not cruel tyrants (and point out that rebellions and kingdoms unwilling to ally with/submit to the Realm would be less common if the Realm was less oppressive). Gold Faction pragmatists who see Solars or Lunars as the most likely way to keep Creation safe, and are willing to let them become as awful tyrants as the Empress is and exploit them ruthlessly, or manipulate them to spend their lives fighting Fae instead of Sidereals (and die frequently). Independents of both philosophical stripes -- pragmatists who will use whoever is most useful at the moment to accomplish whatever goal and betray them later, idealists who believe Sidereals' sole responsibility is Fate (and maybe ____ other thing) and them playing kingmakers is what's wrong with Creation today. That creates 3x as many options for characters as you've got here.<br /> <br /> <br /> You don't want them defined solely by opinion about who should rule the world... neither do I. Their hyper-focus on [killing or saving] Anathema is my biggest criticism of canon Sidereals.<br /> <br /> So give them more to care about! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are Exigents and Getimians and who knows what else in 3E. What are their ideas for interacting with those? There are 3 realms outside of Fate which pose significant and unknown threats to Creation, one of which somehow caused the Great Contagion, which smart Sidereals would pay a <i><b>lot </b></i>of attention to and spend some resources to try to watch/spy on/maybe fight; they probably disagree about how best to do that, for each of the 3 realms. There would be Sidereals who are either Independent or nominally part of a Faction, but who focus on one of these other issues instead. With so few Sidereals, there might not be any two who agree about all of the big issues facing them... so maybe there aren't 2 Factions, as such. But there sure would be disagreement about the big ideas, and coalitions of the like-minded around specific major 'global' issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-20-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:58:00-07:00","id":894781,"title":"","content":"Okay- so you'd like to see more in the way of political dissent played up in the history, then? Alternate courses that Sidereals have tried to use to control the world, times they've pulled back from supporting the Wyld Hunt, that sort of thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:32:23-07:00","id":894806,"title":"","content":"Alternate courses they <i>could</i> have tried that some of them want to try, but don't have enough political support to accomplish. I just can't wrap my head around unanimity among humans. Even in totalitarian societies which strongly devalue individualism, there's <i><b>some</b></i> dissent about big issues.<br /> <br /> Plus it's boring if PC options are so limited. You're always required to do and support XYZ, because there's never been dissent. Like when anyone suggests all Lunars are united about X and Y even though they're spread over the entire Threshold and stuff. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I think Lunars are boring anyway.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> I have also had a lot of thoughts yesterday about the Great Curse which I was pondering the whole time I was away from home, which I let myself get sidetracked from talking about. The idea of Paradox as the micro, PC-level manifestation of the Curse seems to fit well with my own vague suggestion of how it could work on a large scale. Having Paradox be the micro-scale form of the Curse (instead of having... a vague lack of mechanics, or putting it down to ST fiat) keeps control of the immediate manifestation in player hands. It also gave me the idea of broadening what Paradox can look like. Sure sometimes you lose the ability to interact physically with solid objects... but sometimes everybody you meet is irritated with you for no apparent reason. Subtle Paradox effects that aren't &quot;physics break down&quot;. I admit I have a slightly silly view of Paradox, though.<br /> <br /> I had an idea of how relations between Sidereals and other Exalted started to go wrong in the First Age. Solars and Lunars gradually stopped listening to Sidereal advice. The Sidereals thought that was arrogance, and arrogance was certainly a <i><b>big</b></i> part of it... but the other Exalted also started to distrust Sidereal advice because their plans kept backfiring! Yet there was always an external cause that the Sidereals could point to that did it, because their own decisions were often only indirectly, vaguely, subtly at fault.<br /> <br /> Make the Curse subtle enough, and it's no longer necessary to say Exalted are <b><i>incapable</i></b> of noticing the Curse. They haven't yet because... it's just legitimately <i><b>really hard</b></i> to tell. That accomplishes two things: for STs who want the Curse to be incurable and/or not focus on fixing it, it makes it harder to notice, and &quot;Duh, it was right in front of you!&quot; is no longer a thing. For those STs and players who want to tell a story about breaking the Curse, it's possible for any type of Exalt, including Sidereals, to finally realize something funky's happening and try to do something.<br /> <br /> The only difficulty I have with the Paradox approach is that somebody would have noticed when suddenly these fate glitches started happening after the Primordial War, which had never happened before. There needs to be some wrong-but-quite-plausible explanation for that change that First Age Sidereals settled upon. (The easy one is that without the Primordials and Maidens directly controlling the Loom, it just isn't quite as smooth. Hey, Sidereals and Spiders aren't perfect.) Not like Paradox is a super-big problem... by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-20-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:44:12-07:00","id":894854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894806#post894806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternate courses they <i>could</i> have tried that some of them want to try, but don't have enough political support to accomplish. I just can't wrap my head around unanimity among humans. Even in totalitarian societies which strongly devalue individualism, there's <i><b>some</b></i> dissent about big issues.<br /> <br /> Plus it's boring if PC options are so limited. You're always required to do and support XYZ, because there's never been dissent. Like when anyone suggests all Lunars are united about X and Y even though they're spread over the entire Threshold and stuff. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I think Lunars are boring anyway.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly agree with most of this, and will bear these thoughts in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894806#post894806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only difficulty I have with the Paradox approach is that somebody would have noticed when suddenly these fate glitches started happening after the Primordial War, which had never happened before. There needs to be some wrong-but-quite-plausible explanation for that change that First Age Sidereals settled upon. (The easy one is that without the Primordials and Maidens directly controlling the Loom, it just isn't quite as smooth. Hey, Sidereals and Spiders aren't perfect.) Not like Paradox is a super-big problem... by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... this ties into my thoughts on how to ensure Rakan Thulio and the Sidereals can both make compelling cases for protecting / destroying Destiny.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Loom of Fate -&gt; Destiny planned by Heaven -&gt; Potential for paradoxes and for Heaven abusing Destiny for fun and profit, but also acts to limit the intervention of the Gods en masse within Creation.<br /> Without the Loom of Fate -&gt; Creation becomes more vulnerable to external attack and internal divine depredations, falling into an age of savagry not seen since before the dawn of the First Age.<br /> <br /> Both sides have pros and cons; Rakan Thulio believes that the subtle interference of Heaven is an abomination; if the Gods would abuse men, they should have to do so face to face. The the existence of Paradox proves what a gross idea the Loom is. That the Sidereals, as the Agents of Destiny, are complicit in the attrocities that Heaven plans and they enforce.<br /> The Sidereals (by and large) believe that returning to an age of horrifying savagry isn't really in anyone's best interest, and the Loom of Fate and the planning of Heaven is the best alternative available. Rakan Thulio would burn the house and salt the foundations because of a few broken windows.<br /> <br /> (That's the short form, anywho)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:00:57-07:00","id":894868,"title":"","content":"I do share with you the concern about Sidereals being <b><i>focused</i></b> too much on the Solar Question.<br /> <br /> And Rakan Thulio... if you or the devs can manage to make his Destroy Heaven!! crusade look at all sympathetic and not-insane, I'll be impressed. I mean, even most of the <b><i>Yozis</i></b> probably want to keep the Loom of Fate in place, once they regain control over it.<br /> <br /> Like, what does he want to replace the Loom of Fate? Anything? Would physical laws just break down without it, or would they just continue because they're built into Creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:33:09-07:00","id":894897,"title":"","content":"I head canon that he doesn't want to destroy the Loom, but control it. Destroying the Loom would be like a hacker destroying the internet. It would crippled him as much as the Sidereals. <br /> <br /> I have some vague ideas of paradox aging Sidereals. They still live for 5000 years but they look old. This fits with the old wise man themes of the splat. A young looking Sidereal is one who has been careful of paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:36:58-07:00","id":894901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/894035-sidereals-wfhl-pondering-the-rest-of-the-work?p=894868#post894868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do share with you the concern about Sidereals being <b><i>focused</i></b> too much on the Solar Question.<br /> <br /> And Rakan Thulio... if you or the devs can manage to make his Destroy Heaven!! crusade look at all sympathetic and not-insane, I'll be impressed. I mean, even most of the <b><i>Yozis</i></b> probably want to keep the Loom of Fate in place, once they regain control over it.<br /> <br /> Like, what does he want to replace the Loom of Fate? Anything? Would physical laws just break down without it, or would they just continue because they're built into Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what the Devs are planning, mind, so this is purely my speculation.<br /> <br /> Premise: Desiring a course of action that would result in the destruction of Creation will paint you as a crazy villain.<br /> Premise: Rakan Thulio's perspective will not paint him as a crazy villain for wanting to destroy Fate.<br /> Therefore, his desire to destroy Fate cannot result in the assumed destruction of Creation.<br /> <br /> Premise: A status quo in which the freedom, happiness and dignity of the people are significantly constrained or reduced is going to make those who support that status quo look morally questionable, at best- and more likely like quisling villains.<br /> Premise: The default Sidereal perspective will not paint them as quisling villains for wanting to preserve Fate.<br /> Therefore, the default Sidereal perspective to preserve Fate must be sufficient to make their desire rational.<br /> <br /> My speculation is essentially that the Loom of Fate and Heaven's Five Year Plan is sort of a compromise arrangement.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, the Loom didn't exist, and the Gods walked Creation freely. They were charged with the preservation of Creation from external threats, but otherwise given dominion over the world. The role of the Maidens, at this time, was to direct the Gods to where they would be most needed to preserve Creation, and means that when Heaven dictates something to happen, it becomes more likely to happen.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, while the Gods are less alien than their creators, they are still far removed from humanity, and their causes and cares could casually crush common folk. Many were benevolent, but many would also slack strange hungers and alien lusts upon mankind, forces against which humans were largely helpless.<br /> <br /> Then came the Exaltation, the war, and the dawn of the First Age. The Maidens desired to join the rest of the Incarnae in playing the Games of Divinity- but their prophetic insight was still needed to keep Creation safe. The Small Gods were eager to dominate the world- but the Sun had given the Creation-Ruling Mandate to the Exalted for their service. The Loom of Fate was created as a compromise. Heaven plans the weave of destiny, which is half-description and half-prescription. Where the pattern corresponds to Creation, the Gods are limited in the degree to which they can interfere. The greater the deviations, the more freedom the Gods have- nominally to repair what has gone wrong, but there's little hard enforcement on that front- and see previous comment re: 'strange hunters', 'alien lusts'.<br /> <br /> Creation would continue without the Loom of Fate. Fate does not represent natural law, and Destiny is the proper term for &quot;Heaven's intentions towards Creation&quot;. Because the Loom of Fate is, to a degree, pre-scriptive as well as descriptive (to be self-healing from small deviations), the existance of the Loom allows for Paradoxes to occur. <br /> <br /> The Sidereals are troubleshooters who go to fix the weave when it's gone wrong, to act as the direct agents of Heaven on Earth, and to punch Gods that have gone rogue and criminal.<br /> <br /> According to the Sidereals, Creation with the Gods unrestrained would be an age of savagery such has not been known since before the First Age- and it is the function of the Loom of Fate to act as that constraint.<br /> <br /> According to Rakan Thulio, humanity would be better served in an age of savagery than one in which a corrupt Heaven dictates who lives, who dies, who loves, who hates. Men suffer in bondage now- at least then they would suffer in freedom.<br /> <br /> According to the Sidereals, Rakan Thulio doesn't give two shits about the suffering he would impose on humanity; he would burn down the house and salt the earth because the man he loved loved another.<br /> <br /> According to Rakan Thulio, the Sidereals are complicit in every atrocity of Fate's design, every innocent suffering, every wicked deed which is rewarded.<br /> <br /> Some Sidereals can look at Rakan Thulio's arguement, look at Creation, and conclude that he's right. Maybe he *does* have some other way to control the Gods. Maybe he *can* get rid of the influence of a corrupt Heaven. Things are so bad, maybe any alternative is better.<br /> <br /> Some Getimians look at the Sidereal's arguement, look at Creation, and conclude they are right. The Gods unrestrained would be a never-ending disaster for humanity. Better to reform Heaven, to soften the blows of Fate, than to drench their own hands in the torrents of blood that unleashing that hell would cause.<br /> <br /> At least- that's my current line of thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:41:16-07:00","id":894956,"title":"","content":"...what if they're both right?<br /> Fate is tyrannical sometimes... but aren't we talking about a guy who is tormenting every reincarnation of that one Solar just for revenge? (I don't have the Visiting Flare comic so correct me if I'm wrong here.)<br /> <br /> In more seriousness, that looks really interesting and cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","cus